2. Preliminaries

Environment. The external world is a Markov decision process (MDP) with state space \mathcal{X}, action space \mathcal{A}, transition kernel P^e(x' \mid x,a), reward function R^e(x,a), and discount factor \gamma \in [0,1). The agent possesses an internal cognitive state s \in \mathcal{S}, a Polish space, which encodes all possessed information: belief about the external state, retrieved memories, reasoning context, etc.

Cognitive operations. A primitive cognitive operation o \in \mathcal{O}_0 is a tuple (T_o, c, \tau), where T_o(s' \mid s) is a Markov kernel on \mathcal{S}, c(s,o) \ge 0 is a non‑negative computational cost, and \tau(s,o) \ge 1 is a strictly positive integer duration (in discrete time steps). Applying operation o in state s produces a new internal state s' \sim T_o(\cdot \mid s) after \tau(s,o) steps. The set \mathcal{O}_0 of primitive operations is finite. The agent may also choose to stop and execute an external action; stopping incurs zero duration and zero cost.

Value functions. Let V^* : \mathcal{S} \to \mathbb{R} be the optimal state‑value function when the agent can interleave internal operations and external actions, defined as the unique bounded solution of the Bellman equation

V^*(s) = \max\Bigl\{\, U(s),\; \max_{o\in\mathcal{O}_0} \bigl( \gamma^{\tau(s,o)}\, \mathbb{E}[V^*(s') \mid s, o] - c(s,o) \bigr) \Bigr\},
\tag{1}

where U(s) = \max_{a\in\mathcal{A}} \mathbb{E}[R^e(x,a) \mid s] is the value of stopping and acting immediately (under the current belief). Existence and uniqueness of V^* follow from the Banach fixed‑point theorem because the right‑hand side is a \gamma-contraction in the sup‑norm (since \tau(s,o) \ge 1).

Future Value (FV). For any operation o (primitive or composite), its Q‑value and Future Value are

Q(s,o) = \gamma^{\tau(s,o)}\, \mathbb{E}[V^*(s') \mid s, o] - c(s,o), \qquad
\mathrm{FV}(o; s) = Q(s,o) - U(s).
\tag{2}

An operation is worth executing in state s iff \mathrm{FV}(o; s) > 0. The optimal meta‑policy selects an operation with maximal positive FV; if none exists, it stops and acts externally.

